# Anti Social

<!-- l4: assume:Person -->

**1.** In this Act, “Person” denotes a type.

<!-- l4: assume:is authorised -->

**2.** In this Act, “is authorised” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:Receiver -->

**3.** In this Act, “Receiver” denotes a type.

<!-- l4: assume:is an individual aged 16 or over -->

**4.** In this Act, “is an individual aged 16 or over” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:is a body -->

**5.** In this Act, “is a body” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:Effect -->

**6.** In this Act, “Effect” denotes a type.

<!-- l4: assume:EffectTarget -->

**7.** In this Act, “EffectTarget” denotes a type.

<!-- l4: assume:is detrimental -->

**8.** In this Act, “is detrimental” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:is of a persistent or continuing nature -->

**9.** In this Act, “is of a persistent or continuing nature” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:affects the quality of life of those in the locality -->

**10.** In this Act, “affects the quality of life of those in the locality” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: assume:Conduct -->

**11.** In this Act, “Conduct” denotes a type.

<!-- l4: assume:conduct -->

**12.** In this Act, “conduct” denotes a function yielding a Conduct.

<!-- l4: assume:effect -->

**13.** In this Act, “effect” denotes a function yielding an Effect.

<!-- l4: assume:is unreasonable -->

**14.** In this Act, “is unreasonable” denotes a function yielding a BOOLEAN.

<!-- l4: decide:may issue a community protection notice -->

**15.** In relation to a Person “person” and a Receiver “receiver”, may issue a community protection notice if—

    (a) is authorised with person;

    (b) any of the following applies—

        (i) is an individual aged 16 or over with receiver; or

        (ii) is a body with receiver;

    (c) is detrimental with the effect;

    (d) is of a persistent or continuing nature with the effect;

    (e) affects the quality of life of those in the locality with the effect; and

    (f) is unreasonable with the conduct.

For the purposes of this provision—

“the conduct” means conduct with receiver;

“the effect” means effect with the conduct;

